  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Some readers prefer help carrying or locating books, and a helper can provide it without requiring a reason.\", \"decision\": \"How should readers request extra assistance?\", \"goal\": \"Keep books moving and make the afternoon service easier to use without excluding readers who arrive without an appointment.\", \"problem\": \"A small library becomes crowded during afternoon pickups and returns. It has a request sheet, adjustable pickup windows, a few trained helpers, labeled shelves, and enough room to separate several activities. Staff want a practical plan that preserves walk-in access. Each decision below concerns a different part of the service; none requires exclusive use of all helpers or space.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nStaff offer assistance at collection and pass accepted requests to the helper’s list. Help is offered at the point where carrying or locating difficulties become clear.\nA helper offers assistance at arrival and records accepted requests on a list. Readers can choose help after seeing what they need that day.\nReaders request assistance when choosing a pickup window, and staff place the request on the helper’s list. The helper can be available when those readers arrive."
    }
